<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="5a4a80d0-2d4c-5a09-b512-62117e6e5925" activityNameId="cee4efcb-8a70-5fec-a89f-552dff44c5e3" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Mischmetal, primary, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Mischmetal, primary, at plant
Production of Mischmetal from bastnaesite by wet chemical attack and fused salt electrolysis. The product contains 53% Ce, 21% La, 17% Nd, 6% Pr, 0.2% Sm, the rest consistin of Eu, Gd and others. The overall quality of the data is poor. It however may be used as alloying constituent in HSLA steels, nodular iron and hydrogen storage in metal hydride batteries (LaNi5).This dataset is not to be used when mischmetal is a substantial part of the system modelled ;
CAS number: 008049-20-5; 
Synonyms: cerium mischmetal, rare earth mischmetal, misch metal; 
UUID: b5cd8fc8-fb6e-3a58-b36d-7a2a6bf90773
Includes the basic raw materials consumed and energy for precipitation reaction, filtration and drying. No direct emissions or infrastructure are included.
Location: This dataset production facilities scattered over the world. Most upstream processes such as electricity demand and chemicals consumption are approximated with datasets for European situation.
Technology: Production from bastnaesite concentrate that is converted to its chloride and reduced with fused salt electrolysis. Electrolysis approximated with processes from aluminium industry.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature 
Extrapolations: see Geography and Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: This dataset bases on old process description and rough approximation.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_b5cd8fc8-fb6e-3a58-b36d-7a2a6bf90773.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="f4808887-5a57-5892-975e-ba0565a93e23" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
